From 9a7b5dbca781c07862136b759f4d904ba633a0f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mertcanekiz <ekiz.mertcan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 19:05:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: DP-IN v4: replay the macOS 13.5 DP-IN bring-up captured
 with the m1n1 hypervisor

Ground truth: reports/usb4-dpin-v3/HV-TRACE-FINDINGS.md (run 8, LG UltraFine
on ATC1). Differences from v3, in the order the AP does them under macOS:

- appledrm: map the ADT "atc-dpin" bridge blocks (new DT nodes atc1_dpin0/1,
  dcpext "apple,tbt-dpin"); write 0x08=3 and ack 0x04/0x00 before connectTo;
  clear DPTX_INACTIVE inside DPTX_APCALL_ACTIVATE (was a /dev/mem hack);
  connectTo unk=0xb0101, no validateConnection; answer GET_SUPPORTS_HPD=1 and
  send hotPlugDetectChangeOccurred right after ACTIVATE (before link config);
  enable the display crossbar only inside SET_LINK_RATE after the PHY PCLK is
  up; tear it down (DPTX_INACTIVE 1 -> 0) in WILL_CHANGE_LINK_CONFIG and clear
  0x08 in DEACTIVATE; echo SET_TILED_DISPLAY_HINTS untouched; never
  phy_set_mode the USB4/TBT PHY; dpin_prime_rate defaults to 0.
- phy-apple-atc: dpin_mode=1 (default) programs the AUSPLL exactly like
  AppleT8103TypeCPhy::configureDPTunnelMode: RBR VCO (count 0x21c, no
  fraction), pclk_div_sel 5, vclk_op_divn 2, refbufclk divider 1, APB command
  0x2000, only DPTX_PCLK1_SELECT, byte clock left in reset; link rate 0 runs
  unconfigureDPTunnelMode (drop CLKOUT_MASTER drivers, APB command 3).
  dpin_mode=2 keeps the v3 behaviour.
- module params to A/B each delta at runtime: appledrm dpin_validate,
  dpin_connect_unk, dpin_hpd_after_activate, dpin_prime_rate; phy_apple_atc
  dpin_mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
